{
  "id": "cued-speech",
  "term": "cued speech",
  "definition": "Cued speech is a communication method used in speech and language rehabilitation that adds hand cues to spoken language so visually similar speech sounds can be told apart. It combines specific handshapes for consonants and hand positions near the face for vowels to support lipreading and improve phonological decoding, especially for children with hearing impairment.",
